, "uuid": "1ATCNPK4dX", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 46, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8791103, "raw_content": "", "author": "1DontTreadOnMe1", "created": 1787286476581, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "upside-downPHflag", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATCNPK4dX.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/Hannibal9972485/status/2090523652705947985", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "These FALSE arrests and stops starting to make sense. Flock is feeding the police ALERTS based off of altered, degraded, low-resolution copies of license plate data ALERTS .", "last_comment_created": 1787291440749, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 2, "score_up": 46, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": [{"width": 1234, "heightRatio": 165, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HQMILi2WwAAfcWY.jpg", "height": 2048}, {"width": 1010, "heightRatio": 196, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HQMILizXwAAcZ6q.jpg", "height": 1986}, {"width": 1290, "heightRatio": 94, "url": "https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HQMILi4XIAAW6Kb.jpg", "height": 1222}], "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 24, "created": 1787254653000, "id": "2090523652705947985", "video": false, "poll": false, "user": {"profilePicture": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1815607118851903488/nTeODv3f_normal.jpg", "displayName": "Hannibal999", "username": "Hannibal9972485"}, "content": "These FALSE arrests and stops starting to make sense. Flock is feeding the police ALERTS \ud83d\udea8 based off of altered, degraded, low-resolution copies of license plate data ALERTS .\n\nIf POLICE  want a more high-resolution original file with the metadata, the police department is", "parentTweet": false, "likes": 467}}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1ATCNPK4hg", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 43, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8791114, "raw_content": "Surveillance Technology: FalcoNet\nCognyte is the manufacturer of FalcoNet, a controversial cell-site simulator (IMSI catcher) used for mobile phone surveillance. \n\nFunctionality: FalcoNet mimics a legitimate cell tower, forcing nearby mobile phones (2G through 5G) to connect to it instead of the carrier network. This allows operators to capture device identifiers (IMSI/IMEI) and location data from all phones in range, not just specific targets. Cognyte is used for surveillance primarily through two distinct methods: active signal interception using hardware devices and passive data fusion using software analytics. \n\nActive Signal Interception (IMSI Catchers)\nThe most direct form of surveillance is conducted using FalcoNet, an IMSI-catcher (also known as a cell-site simulator) similar to the widely known \"Stingray.\" \n\nMechanism: The device mimics a legitimate cell tower, broadcasting a signal strong enough to force nearby mobile phones (2G through 5G) to disconnect from real towers and connect to it instead. \nData Collection: Once connected, FalcoNet harvests unique identifiers (IMSI, IMEI) and precise location data from every device in range, not just specific targets.  This creates a \"dragnet\" effect, collecting data on innocent bystanders alongside suspects.\nDeployment: The system is highly portable and modular. Recent contracts reveal it is being deployed in:\nVehicles: Concealed inside police SUVs (e.g., Chevy Tahoes used by Texas and Florida police) to track movements while driving.\nAirborne: Mounted on helicopters for wide-area surveillance, such as monitoring migration routes.\nPortable: Packaged in backpacks for foot patrols or tactical operations. \nStealth: The technology operates silently without the user's knowledge, and the hardware can be hidden behind false vehicle roofs to remain visually indistinguishable from standard patrol cars", "author": "RYTHMICRIOT", "created": 1787287550512, "profile_picture": "unkHmy325PwW", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "bobbybadass", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "And you thought flock cameras were bad. Look into Cognyte/FalcoNet", "last_comment_created": 1787312275500, "content": "<p>Surveillance Technology: FalcoNet\nCognyte is the manufacturer of FalcoNet, a controversial cell-site simulator (IMSI catcher) used for mobile phone surveillance.</p>\n<p>Functionality: FalcoNet mimics a legitimate cell tower, forcing nearby mobile phones (2G through 5G) to connect to it instead of the carrier network. This allows operators to capture device identifiers (IMSI/IMEI) and location data from all phones in range, not just specific targets. Cognyte is used for surveillance primarily through two distinct methods: active signal interception using hardware devices and passive data fusion using software analytics.</p>\n<p>Active Signal Interception (IMSI Catchers)\nThe most direct form of surveillance is conducted using FalcoNet, an IMSI-catcher (also known as a cell-site simulator) similar to the widely known &quot;Stingray.&quot;</p>\n<p>Mechanism: The device mimics a legitimate cell tower, broadcasting a signal strong enough to force nearby mobile phones (2G through 5G) to disconnect from real towers and connect to it instead.\nData Collection: Once connected, FalcoNet harvests unique identifiers (IMSI, IMEI) and precise location data from every device in range, not just specific targets.  This creates a &quot;dragnet&quot; effect, collecting data on innocent bystanders alongside suspects.\nDeployment: The system is highly portable and modular. Recent contracts reveal it is being deployed in:\nVehicles: Concealed inside police SUVs (e.g., Chevy Tahoes used by Texas and Florida police) to track movements while driving.\nAirborne: Mounted on helicopters for wide-area surveillance, such as monitoring migration routes.\nPortable: Packaged in backpacks for foot patrols or tactical operations.\nStealth: The technology operates silently without the user's knowledge, and the hardware can be hidden behind false vehicle roofs to remain visually indistinguishable from standard patrol cars</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 4, "score_up": 43, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATCNPK5Ee", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 31, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8791190, "raw_content": "", "author": "catsfive", "created": 1787293683541, "profile_picture": "mz8KUa00CFwJ", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "KnighTshade", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "media.scored.co", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1ATCNPK5Ee.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://media.scored.co/post/eqEm1I0DPZME.jpeg", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [{"reference": "/scale/doXIIQIgGLkf809F.jpeg",